WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:08.000
[Traditional Sámi joik — a vocal expression
that evokes a person, animal, or place]

2
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:18.000
[The joik does not describe — it embodies.
Each melody is unique to its subject.]

3
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:35.000
[Joik is one of the oldest vocal traditions
in Europe, predating written history.]

4
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:55.000
[Once forbidden in schools and churches,
joik survived through quiet practice.]

5
00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:15.000
[Today, Sámi communities are reclaiming joik
as a living expression of identity and land.]

6
00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:32.000
[Northern Sámi — spoken by approximately
20,000 people across Norway, Sweden, and Finland]

7
00:01:33.000 --> 00:02:10.000
[A voice carried across the Arctic,
still breathing, still being heard.]
